  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-03-13T13:17:39.973Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Anyone who ever tried vehicles in VRChat knows that they generate motion sickness due to added head rotation. There is currently no option for chairs/stations to move and rotate the players but not rotate the head, so that the players can rotate their heads themselve as usual. This makes vehicles in VRChat unusable for VR users, but it would be simple to solve this by not affecting the head rotation from the chair rotation.\nWhile it is possible to make a chair that almost doesn't rotate the player, it does look weird if the vehicle rotates without the chair/player and this isn't easy to implement either and still has lots of problems over a chair that is simply fixed to the vehicle.\nIt would be the best to disable the added head rotation from a chair locally on demand, so that only VR users can do it.\nI'm a VR game dev and I made lots of demos where players are moved but not rotated and tried them on other people new to VR. Allowing them to rotate themselves prevents motion sickness in vehicles. I made a similar demo in VRChat but since the chair/avatar isn't rotated there as well, it looks just weird. An option added to VRC stations to disable the head rotation would also be fine.",
